+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document, not the whole new version. The library can apply a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) but cannot produce one.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` when applied with `applyPatch`.
+- The patch is minimal in size: it descends into objects and arrays and describes only the places that differ.
+- Array item insertions and removals yield a single `add`/`remove` of that item; an item moved within an array yields a `move` (or a `remove` plus `add`) and does not rewrite the items in between.
+- Neither input is modified, and the patch shares no mutable structure with them.
+- Document the function in `README.md`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch-diff`: producing a minimal JSON Patch from two JSON documents.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New module `src/diff.ts`, re-exported from `src/index.ts`; tests in `test/`; `README.md` section.
+- No change to existing behavior, no new dependency.
